      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T19:25:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not \"that an unwieldly\" parameter, but is it that unwieldly to add logsPrefix to the config?\n\n1. Why are we changing the `run` function signatures if we don\u0027t have to?\n2. In general, passing a string (where there is expectation about it being a *prefix*, especially) is more confusing than passing along something more \"strongly typed\" (such as something that is very clearly a *Prefix* string). Since it\u0027s overkill to create a type for a \"logs prefix\", it\u0027s less confusing to lump the prefix into one of the ctx or config tuples.\n\nThese concerns are magnified when we consider that it should be *very* clear what the signature of each `run` function is. Thankfully build.Context and build.Config are inherently very clear, because there should really only be one instance of these objects. A `logsPrefix` string less so.\n\nMost run() functions don\u0027t even care about accessing the logsPrefix value, so it makes sense to lump into config objects that are propagated instead.",
      "parentUuid": "6b5ba3f1_2a286be7",
      "revId": "6a41c48559752bfa5778d609f7b5a1abe1e0083e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
